---
const pains = [
  {
    before: "You've tried ChatGPT, maybe Copilot.",
    after: "But copy-pasting prompts isn't a workflow. It's a workaround.",
  },
  {
    before: "You've seen demos of AI agents and automations.",
    after: "But nobody explains how to connect them to your CRM, your inbox, or your actual data.",
  },
  {
    before: "You've talked to agencies and dev shops.",
    after: "They quote six figures and six months for something you just need to work.",
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="problem">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" data-animate>
      <span class="eyebrow">Sound familiar?</span>
      <h2>The AI hype is everywhere.<br />The help isn't.</h2>
      <p>
        You run a business, not an engineering team. You know AI could save
        you hours every week – but the gap between the buzz and a working
        tool feels impossible to cross on your own.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="pain-list">
      {
        pains.map((pain, i) => (
          <div class="pain-item" data-animate style={`--stagger: ${i + 1}`}>
            <p class="pain-before">{pain.before}</p>
            <p class="pain-after">{pain.after}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <p class="pain-resolve" data-animate style="--stagger: 5">
      That's exactly the gap SMBuddy fills. You describe what you need – we
      build it, in your stack, and hand you the keys.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .pain-list {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-2xl);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .pain-item {
    padding: var(--space-lg) var(--space-xl);
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-purple);
  }

  .pain-before {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .pain-after {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .pain-resolve {
    max-width: 600px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .pain-item {
      padding: var(--space-md) var(--space-lg);
    }
  }
</style>
